-- Smoothcomp organizer aliases activated 2026-10-06 (EXC-166 follow-up): the eleven
--
-- APPLIED RECORD. Founder's word, 2026-10-05: "yes add the 11 non-grappling
-- organizations we want this to be a master list of all events locally".
-- These are the eleven held back on 2026-10-04 only because they are not
-- grappling (scout/terms-reviews/smoothcomp-aliases-2026-10-04.sql). These
-- exact statements were applied to production (almanac) on 2026-10-07 around
-- 04:52 UTC (the night of 2026-10-06 in America/Chicago), then to
-- almanac-staging. Do not re-apply: host is UNIQUE, so a second run fails on
-- purpose. Production went from 28 to 39 active aliases.
--
-- Cleared the same way as the 22, on 2026-10-07 04:41-04:49 UTC, one 11-second
-- clock across all Smoothcomp hosts, pinned user agent, redirects recorded and
-- never followed, terms page first (2026-09-26 crawl-law ruling):
--   1. /en/agreements: 404 on all eleven (no subdomain terms).
--   2. robots.txt: byte-identical to smoothcomp.com's (sha256 312e3e13...) on all eleven.
--   3. /en: a 302 whose Location is the federation listing path, on all eleven.
--   4. That listing, through the Scout's own parseListingEvents (current main):
--      HTTP 200 on all eleven; events read: allamericansambo 1, allthingsjudo 4,
--      americanjudo 5, judocomp 2, ktmdka 1, mdl 0, nanka 4, tba-sa 2,
--      usajudo 5, usjf 3, wbcmtusa 1.
-- One departure from the 22's rule, on the founder's word: mdl listed zero
-- upcoming events that day. Its path came from its own /en redirect and
-- answered 200, so it is activated; the nightly crawl reports zero drafts for
-- it until the organizer lists an event. Each row's terms_reasoning says so.
--
-- What members see: these organizers run judo, sambo and other non-grappling
-- events. The app has no sport field yet, so the Tournament Master will offer
-- them alongside grappling events (founder: "a master list of all events").
--
